HST Office: own Windows Installer UpgradeCode, and removal of the betas installed under LibreOffice's.

The HSTOffice product set no CODEFILENAME, so its MSI used LibreOffice's UpgradeCode from
codes.txt. Windows Installer then took every installed LibreOffice (3.3 and later, all above
1.0.0) for a newer HST Office and refused to install, and a later LibreOffice install would
remove HST Office as an older LibreOffice.

- codes_hst.txt holds HST Office's own UpgradeCode, which must never change. The ProductCode
  stays generated per build, so every release is a major upgrade as upstream does.
- HST Office 1.0.0 beta 1 to 4 were installed under LibreOffice's code (ProductVersion 1.0.0.1).
  New product variables LEGACYUPGRADECODE / LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMIN / LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMAX
  add one Upgrade row that removes those during the upgrade, limited to [1.0.0.0, 1.0.1.0).
  Windows Installer compares only the first three version fields, and LibreOffice for Windows
  never had an MSI below 3.3, so the row matches HST's 1.0.0.x and no LibreOffice. It uses the
  OLDPRODUCTS property, so RemoveExistingProducts and the install-path migration see the old
  beta as they see an earlier release under the new code; it is never a NEWPRODUCTS (downgrade)
  row, so an installed LibreOffice cannot block the installation.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0); codes_hst.txt is new HST data
under the same license as the file next to it (MPL-2.0).

--- a/instsetoo_native/util/openoffice.lst.in
+++ b/instsetoo_native/util/openoffice.lst.in
@@ -101,12 +101,16 @@
             LICENSENAME @LICENSE@
             ROOTMODULEGID gid_Module_Root
             GLOBALPATCHFILEGID gid_File_Txt_Patchfiles
             SPELLCHECKERFILE spellchecker_selection.txt
             CHANGETARGETDIR 1
             PATCHCODEFILE ooo_patchcodes.txt
+            CODEFILENAME codes_hst.txt
+            LEGACYUPGRADECODE {4B17E523-5D91-4E69-BD96-7FD81CFA81BB}
+            LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMIN 1.0.0.0
+            LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMAX 1.0.1.0
         }
         active          1
         compression     5
         script          setup_osl
         downloadname    HSTOffice_{productversion}_{os}_install_{languages}
         langpackdownloadname    HSTOffice_{productversion}_languagepack_{os}_install_{languages}
--- a/solenv/bin/modules/installer/windows/upgrade.pm
+++ b/solenv/bin/modules/installer/windows/upgrade.pm
@@ -48,6 +48,22 @@
     $newline = $installer::globals::upgradecode . "\t" . $installer::globals::msiproductversion . "\t" . "\t" . "\t" . "2" . "\t" . "\t" . "NEWPRODUCTS" . "\n";
     push(@upgradetable, $newline);
 
+    # Builds installed under another UpgradeCode (LEGACYUPGRADECODE) are removed too, but only
+    # inside [LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMIN, LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMAX): the range must not reach any
+    # version of the product that owns that code. They are only removed, never detected as newer.
+    if ( $allvariableshashref->{'LEGACYUPGRADECODE'} )
+    {
+        my $legacycode = $allvariableshashref->{'LEGACYUPGRADECODE'};
+        my $legacymin = $allvariableshashref->{'LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMIN'} // "";
+        my $legacymax = $allvariableshashref->{'LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMAX'} // "";
+        if ( $legacycode !~ /^\{[0-9A-F]{8}-[0-9A-F]{4}-[0-9A-F]{4}-[0-9A-F]{4}-[0-9A-F]{12}\}$/ ) { installer::exiter::exit_program("ERROR: LEGACYUPGRADECODE is not an uppercase GUID in braces: $legacycode", "create_upgrade_table"); }
+        if ( uc($legacycode) eq uc($installer::globals::upgradecode) ) { installer::exiter::exit_program("ERROR: LEGACYUPGRADECODE equals the UpgradeCode", "create_upgrade_table"); }
+        if (( $legacymin !~ /^\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+$/ ) || ( $legacymax !~ /^\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+$/ )) { installer::exiter::exit_program("ERROR: LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMIN/MAX must both be set as a.b.c.d", "create_upgrade_table"); }
+        # 257 = msidbUpgradeAttributesMigrateFeatures (1) + msidbUpgradeAttributesVersionMinInclusive (256); the maximum is exclusive.
+        $newline = $legacycode . "\t" . $legacymin . "\t" . $legacymax . "\t" . "\t" . "257" . "\t" . "\t" . "OLDPRODUCTS" . "\n";
+        push(@upgradetable, $newline);
+    }
+
     # Saving the file
 
     my $upgradetablename = $basedir . $installer::globals::separator . "Upgrade.idt";
--- /dev/null
+++ b/instsetoo_native/inc_openoffice/windows/msi_templates/codes_hst.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+#
+# HST Office Windows installer codes (product HSTOffice, CODEFILENAME in openoffice.lst.in).
+#
+# The UpgradeCode identifies HST Office to Windows Installer across all releases. It must never
+# change: every later HST MSI finds and replaces the installed one through it, and it must stay
+# different from LibreOffice's code in codes.txt so that the two can be installed side by side.
+# The ProductCode is not listed here: the installer generates a new one for each build, so
+# every release is a major upgrade.
+#
+
+[UPGRADECODE]
+en-US = "{A1751BCB-2603-4428-A5DE-419B438ECFBC}"
